0\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aattempt_id\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cfrozen_until\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\00\02\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\11PerchAccountError\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01fThe configuration revision: 0 after the constructor, advanced by one\0ain every successful `apply_doc` (whatever it changes, a re-apply of\0athe same document included) and every executed upgrade. Freeze\0achanges, recovery attempts, evidence, and cancellations do not\0aadvance it. Never decreases and never repeats, so unlike `doc_hash` it\0atells A -> B -> A apart.\00\00\00\00\00\08revision\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Apply a policy document \e2\80\94 **the only way authorization changes**.\0aThe shared, immutable infra it uses (the doc compiler, the\0ainterpreter, and the spending limit) is derived from build-time pins\0a(see [`infra`]), never passed in. Brings the installed rules to the\0adocument in one invocation, changing only the rules that differ, and\0areturns the canonical `doc_hash`.\0a\0aAuthorized by the owner (any ordinary rule scoped to the account),\0aor, for a recovery completion only, by the zero-signer recovery rule\0awhose controller checks the exact target. On an account with an\0aadopted controller, the controller's `rcv_sync` classifies the call\0abefore any rule changes and refuses what the profile does not allow\0a(`docs/recovery/spec.md` \c2\a710). `approval_valid_until` is the\0afreshness bound a `Protected` reconfiguration's recorded approvals\0awere given for; it is ignored otherwise.\0a\0aWith `expected_revision`, the call refuses with `StaleRevision`\0aunless the account is still at that [`Self::revision`], so a document\0aprepared agains\00\00\00\09apply_doc\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08doc_json\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\14approval_valid_until\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11expected_revision\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e9\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\0